WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.987
- [Shopper] They are so cute

00:00:01.987 --> 00:00:03.873
and they even smell
like the cereal, y'all.

00:00:03.873 --> 00:00:05.730
- [Narrator] , Crocs the colorful shoe

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.490
that first became popular
in the early 2000s,

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.760
hit its peak in 2021.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.240
The company reported a
record annual revenue

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.340
of $2.3 billion in 2021,

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.220
up over 60% from the previous year.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.880
And its stock reached record highs.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.150
- The past few years for
Crocs has been this moment

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.830
of heavy collaboration, constant releases.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:29.880
They're really trying to put themselves

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.940
in front of people

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.384
that might not have
considered Crocs prior.

00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:34.830
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.610
- [Narrator] The company's
success coincided

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.620
with the pandemic,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.770
leading some to credit the
shoes' popularity to timing,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.100
especially as its stock
price has been dropping

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.300
since the pandemic boom has waned.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.230
But other comfortable footwear brands

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.430
didn't take off the way Crocs did.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:50.930
So how did Crocs make a name

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.470
for itself during the pandemic?

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.520
And how did it find success as one

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.120
of fashion's most divisive shoes?

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.593
This is The Economics of Crocs.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.940
The company was founded in 2002,

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.730
the same year it debuted its classic clog.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.340
The name Crocs was inspired

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.080
by crocodiles who live
on land and in water.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.050
- When Crocs were first released,

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.070
they were intended for a consumer

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.810
that was looking at them
as a functional thing,

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.960
so probably gardeners,
people that were on boats,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.960
people that worked all day on their feet,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.930
people that worked on a line at a kitchen.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:24.570
- [Narrator] Part of what
makes them so functional

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.490
is the material,

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:28.640
a proprietary closed-cell
resin called Croslite

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.970
that's slip resistant,

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.340
lightweight and easy to clean.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.400
- Producing a molded shoe

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.500
is certainly simpler in a lot of ways

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.050
than assembling a sneaker.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.270
The most underrated advantage they have

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.160
over the marketplace

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.230
is that it's clear that they're
able to kind of do things

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.260
that other companies
would not be able to do

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.160
because of their scale

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.970
and because of their
production capabilities.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.670
- [Narrator] Crocs sales tool off.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.920
In the first 3/4 of 2005,

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.280
it sold 4.4 million shoes,

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.563
hitting a revenue of $75 million.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.650
Part of the reason for its initial success

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.400
was that the shoe was easy to get.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.160
It was available at retail stores,

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.360
gift shops and mall kiosks.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.160
In 2006, Crocs purchased Jibbitz,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.780
a company that made small
plastic shoe charms.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.830
That same year, the company went public

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:16.670
and became the largest-ever
US footwear IPO at the time.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.650
But in 2008, in the midst
of the financial crash,

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.803
the company suffered a net
income loss of $185 million.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.450
Though the initial craze had simmered,

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.250
the brand still managed to hang on

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.300
to a relatively large customer base

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.150
over the next few years
thanks to its global presence.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.210
In 2014, Crocs started
making major changes

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.100
to its business model,

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.900
closing dozens of stores,
shifting away from malls

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.360
and turning to online sellers like Amazon.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.940
- Crocs announcing today it
will eliminate nearly 200 jobs

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.040
and close a number of
retail stores as part

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.510
of a restructuring effort.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.940
- [Narrator] The company also cut back

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.480
on the number of styles it
sold by between 30 and 40%,

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.120
and refocused on the classic
clog that made it famous.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.070
The following year,

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.300
Crocs invested in a global marketing push

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.223
to relaunch its brand image.

00:03:03.223 --> 00:03:05.540
(lively music)

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.770
Despite its efforts,

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.550
the company's stock held steady

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.270
until 2020 when the global pandemic hit.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.520
- Prior to people working from home

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.090
and not wearing their dress shoes,

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.120
not wearing their heels,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.250
there was already this rising wave

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.970
of comfort-minded, comfort-first footwear

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.900
that was really becoming more popular.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.980
Of course, that accelerated
during the pandemic.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.150
- [Narrator] The comfort aspect
is what many call the key

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.890
to Crocs' success but
another important factor

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.000
is how easy it is to customize
the shoe with Jibbitz.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.470
You could move them to
different Crocs over time

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.970
as you got a green pair,
a camo pair, a pink pair.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.040
The Jibbitz would stay with
you and they were yours.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:43.430
They were almost like the way
a key chain on a backpack was

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.630
at a certain point.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.240
- [Narrator] This idea of individuality

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.740
and self-expression is one

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.779
that the brand emphasizes
through its marketing campaigns.

00:03:50.779 --> 00:03:52.730
(upbeat music)

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.920
And on social media,

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.970
the uniqueness of the shoe's
design has sparked debate.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.720
- Even going back to Crocs' early days,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.180
there were two warring factions

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.740
of Crocs are ugly and
they're a blight on society,

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.700
and we need to get rid of them.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.710
- I don't care how comfortable
they are, they're ugly.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.990
- And then there were people that said,

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.930
no, they're cute and
they're kind of doughy

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:10.830
and they're fun.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.770
- [Shopper] Look how
freaking cute these are.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.010
- [Narrator] Crocs leaned
into this polarization,

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.240
partnering with celebrities
and well-known brands

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.370
to create limited edition
versions of the classic clog.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.900
- I think that's probably
the biggest shift

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.800
within the fashion
world of the past decade

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.380
is that people truly seem
to design for Instagram

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.640
because you wanna stop
people from scrolling

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.260
and certainly, a show plastered

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.020
with fried chicken does that.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.410
- [Narrator] In 2018, Crocs
says its Balenciaga clog,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.370
an $850 four-inch platform shoe,

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.210
sold out within hours.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.750
And in 2021, Crocs says it partnered

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.810
with more than two dozen
brands, artists and creators

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.330
through collaborations
and license programs.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.710
- Sometimes it was through Jibbitz

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.580
but sometimes it was like these kind

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:57.820
of crazy revamping of what their clog was.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.890
- [Narrator] Constantly
releasing new collaborations

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:01.880
has not only kept Crocs in the press

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.260
but it has also helped it
break into new markets.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.730
- There're like Croc collectors

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.760
that go after every model.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.880
- [Collector] Honey, I am
overflowing with Crocs.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.660
- The same way that Nikes resell

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.590
on website like Stock and eBay,

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.970
Crocs are now reselling.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:17.670
- [Narrator] Crocs and
other comfortable shoes

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.310
may have peaked with the pandemic

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.510
as people begin to migrate back into work

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.700
and consider more traditionalist footwear.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.550
But many others are still
prioritizing comfort.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.960
- We're saying that with a
lot of doughy running sneakers

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:29.880
that people are wearing.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.410
We're seeing that certainly
with the growth of slides

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.220
as a huge business in the luxury market.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.050
- [Narrator] Crocs's stock
has dropped around 60%

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.380
since its November 2021 high.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.740
- I think the market's
nervous about the short term.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:45.249
So we're definitely
seeing supply constraints

00:05:45.249 --> 00:05:47.010
in the first quarter.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.140
- [Narrator] But the company
says its fourth straight year

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.200
of revenue growth is fueled
by continued global demand,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:57.030
and it expects revenue to grow
to over $5 billion by 2026.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.900
- I think that they might
plateau at a certain point.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.700
You can only reach so many
consumers but I think for now,

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:07.020
they have been able to
convince enough consumers

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.170
that they deserve space
within their closet.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.168
- And they gotta have the two fingers.

00:06:11.168 --> 00:06:13.060
(shopper chuckling)

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.727
(playful music)

